    "created_at": "2017-02-08T22:35:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-08T23:05:32Z",
    "body": "I'm looking into this more. We can definitely remove `<button type=\"menu\">`, but once we do that, `<menu type=\"toolbar\">` starts looking pretty useless. I started trying to hack together some acceptable CSS to make the spec's example uses of it look reasonable and it's just a mess. I'm going to remove it entirely; authors can use lists and such.\r\n\r\nEdit: meh, I guess as long as I don't try to make the spec's examples work, we can leave it as an alternative to `<ol>` and `<ul>`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
